  "merits": "Before & After the Prayer: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: Imam 'Ali Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) used to say: Whoever says these words will be added to the group of Muhammad and his Household.\n\nBefore the Opening Takbir: Safwan al-Jammal is reported to have said: I was once with Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.). He directed his face towards the qiblah (for performing a prayer) and said this supplicatory prayer before he uttered the takbirat al-ihram (the opening statement of the ritual prayer).\n\nAfter the Zuhr Prayer: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: Imam 'Ali Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) used to say this supplicatory prayer whenever he accomplished the midday (Zuhr) prayer. He would then prostrate himself and say the second supplicatory prayer.\n\nDua of Imam al-Taqi (a.s.): Imam Muhammad al-Taqi (a.s.) is reported to have said: When you accomplish an obligatory prayer, you may say this supplicatory prayer.\n\nDua of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.): Whenever he accomplished an obligatory prayer, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) would say this supplicatory prayer.\n\nProtection for Self, Family & Home: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: Whoever says these words at every obligatory prayer will have himself, his house, his property and his children under protection."
